==============================================================================
(I.a) THE CONJUGATION  A = (J - I + S)/2  IS EXACT
==============================================================================
  tournaments checked : 5096 ; failures of A = (J - I + S)/2 : 0
  -> the map is exactly the owner's x |-> (1+x)/2, and the -I/2 is the residue
     left by the diagonal, since (1+0)/2 = 1/2 rather than 0.

==============================================================================
(I.b) EVERY TOURNAMENT EIGENVALUE HAS Re >= -1/2
==============================================================================
  A + A^T = J - I, so 2 Re(x* A x) = |sum x_i|^2 - 1 >= -1 on unit x.
  tournaments checked : 4096 ; violations of Re >= -1/2 : 0
  minimum real part seen over all of them : -0.500000000000

==============================================================================
(I.c) REGULAR TOURNAMENTS: every NON-PERRON eigenvalue has Re EXACTLY -1/2
==============================================================================
  For a regular tournament J S = 0, so off the all-ones vector A = (S - I)/2,
  and S has purely imaginary spectrum (THM-1455).  Hence Re = -1/2 exactly.
  n = 3 : Perron = 1.0000 (expect 1.0000) ; other Re = ['-0.500000', '-0.500000'] ; all -1/2 : True
  n = 5 : Perron = 2.0000 (expect 2.0000) ; other Re = ['-0.500000', '-0.500000', '-0.500000', '-0.500000'] ; all -1/2 : True
  n = 7 : Perron = 3.0000 (expect 3.0000) ; other Re = ['-0.500000', '-0.500000', '-0.500000', '-0.500000'] ; all -1/2 : True
  regular tournaments sampled : 8 ; all satisfied the line Re = -1/2.

  So THM-1455's 'char(S) parity-pure, spectrum purely imaginary' reads, in the
  affine coordinate, as 'spec(A) lies on the vertical line Re = -1/2'.  The two
  statements are the SAME fact in the two coordinate systems, and the shift is
  precisely the owner's 1/2.

==============================================================================
(II) THE SAME DICHOTOMY IN THE GMC NULLCONE: sign vs Newton midpoint
==============================================================================
  THM-1540: the nullcone condition is that the CHARGES a-b are all of one strict
  SIGN.  Its L2 step asks whether the support of h straddles d/2 -- the MIDPOINT
  of the Newton segment.  Those are one condition in two coordinates:

  support of h (powers of t) d                charges 2a-d       one-sided = midpoint out
  [0, 1]                     1                [-1, 1]            False / False   agree: True
  [1]                        1                [1]                True / True   agree: True
  [0]                        1                [-1]               True / True   agree: True
  [0, 2]                     2                [-2, 2]            False / False   agree: True
  [2]                        2                [2]                True / True   agree: True
  [0, 1, 2]                  2                [-2, 0, 2]         False / False   agree: True
  [1, 2, 3]                  3                [-1, 1, 3]         False / False   agree: True
  [0, 3]                     3                [-3, 3]            False / False   agree: True

  The two columns agree in every row: 'all charges of one sign' and 'the Newton
  midpoint d/2 lies outside the support' are the same statement.  The charge
  a-b is the SIGN coordinate; the exponent a with midpoint d/2 is the AFFINE
  coordinate; and a - b = 2a - d is exactly the inverse of x |-> (1+x)/2 rescaled.
